  <prompt>After the FR-01 task-agenda answer, render capability-backed follow-on CARDS to open Daily Briefing and Smart To Do — but ONLY if that tab is not already open (reuse the R3 open-tab awareness / workspace-state block). Clicking a card dispatches the single-surface launch from task 022 (via `launchSurface` / `handleSurfaceLaunch`); no duplicate tabs. Cards (persistent act-on items) NOT chips, per ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA; if both cards show, collapse the proactive-card stack behind one disclosure header. Render in `ConversationPane` `transcriptFooter` (~:2889–2910) via `useConsumerChips.tsx`.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. Fluent UI v9 + React 18 expertise; comfortable with the ConversationPane transcriptFooter / useConsumerChips follow-on-card render path, the R3 open-tab awareness (workspace-state) block, and the surfaceLaunch dispatch (launchSurface / handleSurfaceLaunch).</role>
  <goal>After the FR-01 task-agenda answer, capability-backed follow-on CARDS to open Daily Briefing + Smart To Do render ONLY if that tab is not already open (reusing R3 open-tab awareness); clicking dispatches the task-022 single-surface launch with no duplicate tab; the cards are cards (not chips) and a two-card stack collapses under one disclosure header.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-06 — capability-backed Briefing / Smart To Do cards. After the FR-01 grounded task-agenda answer (dep 012), the Assistant offers to open Daily Briefing and Smart To Do. These are persistent act-on items, so per ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA they are CARDS (not chips) and, when multiple proactive cards stack, they collapse behind ONE disclosure header. Follow-on cards render in `ConversationPane` `transcriptFooter` (~:2889–2910) via `useConsumerChips.tsx`. R3 shipped open-tab awareness (a workspace-state block that knows which tabs are open); reuse it to GATE each card — suppress a card when its target tab is already open (no duplicate tab). Clicking a card dispatches the single-surface launch entries added in task 022 (Daily Briefing, Smart To Do) via `launchSurface` / `handleSurfaceLaunch` (~:1245–1312), which routes workspace-tab entries generically through PaneEventBus `widget_load`. This is the card half of E2; task 021 gates the free-string suggestions and task 022 supplies the launch entries.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (transcriptFooter ~:2889–2910 — where follow-on cards render; handleSurfaceLaunch ~:1245–1312 — the launch dispatch; the R3 open-tab-awareness workspace-state block)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/useConsumerChips.tsx (the follow-on-card render path to extend for the two gated cards)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/surfaceHandoff/surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts (the task-022 Daily Briefing + Smart To Do entries the cards dispatch)</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md (cards vs chips; collapse a proactive-card stack behind one disclosure header)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA" scope="cards">Persistent act-on items are CARDS (not chips); when both cards show, collapse the proactive-card stack behind ONE disclosure header; no code in card labels; hover only on clickable regions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="gating">Suppress a card when its target tab is already open (reuse R3 open-tab awareness) — MUST NOT open a duplicate tab.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="launch dispatch">Clicking a card dispatches the single-surface launch from task 022 via `launchSurface` / `handleSurfaceLaunch`; MUST NOT add a per-card code branch (the generic workspace-tab dispatch handles it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021" scope="the card styling">Fluent v9 tokens-only; host-agnostic — MUST NOT regress other ConversationPane / SprkChat consumers or the full-page/widget hosts.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
