  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the R3 open-tab-awareness workspace-state block in ConversationPane to know which tabs (Daily Briefing, Smart To Do) are currently open.</step>
    <step order="2">In `transcriptFooter` (~:2889–2910) via `useConsumerChips.tsx`, render the two follow-on CARDS after the FR-01 answer — but only when the respective tab is closed.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire each card's click to the single-surface launch (task 022 entries) via `launchSurface` / `handleSurfaceLaunch`.</step>
    <step order="4">When both cards show, collapse the proactive-card stack behind ONE disclosure header (ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA).</step>
    <step order="5">Verify no duplicate tab opens and no regression to other ConversationPane / SprkChat consumers.</step>
    <step order="6">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <justification>
    <existing>The `transcriptFooter` / `useConsumerChips` follow-on-card path + R3 open-tab awareness + the task-022 launch entries all exist.</existing>
    <extension>Render two gated cards in the existing footer path and dispatch the existing launch entries — no new card system, no new dispatch.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>After the FR-01 answer the user has no capability-backed way to open Briefing / Smart To Do, or (without gating) opens duplicate tabs.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
